      "title": "Update existing library: io.netty:netty-common:4.1.132.Final",
      "label": "fails-native-image-run",
      "body": "## Additional context and logs\n\n`io.netty:netty-common:4.1.132.Final` resolves to the **netty 5 alpha** metadata directory,\nwhich does not contain the shaded jctools registrations that 4.1.x needs. Any 4.1.x consumer\nthat reaches `io.netty.util.Recycler` now fails at run time.\n\nThis surfaced as a failure of the `org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-common:4.2.1` test suite in\noracle/graal's [Weekly Reachability Metadata Tests](https://github.com/oracle/graal/actions/runs/31984989117/job/95259477773)\n(2026-08-17), but pulsar is only the messenger — the defect is in `io.netty/netty-common`.\n\n### What happens\n\n```\nJUnit Jupiter:ByteBufPairTest:coalescesBothBuffersAndReleasesPair()\n  => org.graalvm.nativeimage.MissingReflectionRegistrationError: Cannot reflectively read or write\n     field 'private volatile long\n     io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.queues.BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueueProducerFields.producerIndex'.\n     To allow this operation, add the following to the 'reflection' section of\n     'reachability-metadata.json' and rebuild the native image:\n\n  {\n    \"type\": \"io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.queues.BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueueProducerFields\",\n    \"fields\": [ { \"name\": \"producerIndex\" } ]\n  }\n\n     com.oracle.svm.core.reflect.MissingReflectionRegistrationUtils.reportAccessedField(MissingReflectionRegistrationUtils.java:80)\n     com.oracle.svm.core.reflect.UnsafeFieldUtil.getFieldOffset(UnsafeFieldUtil.java:48)\n     java.base@25.0.4.1/jdk.internal.misc.Unsafe.objectFieldOffset(Unsafe.java:46)\n     jdk.unsupported@25.0.4.1/sun.misc.Unsafe.objectFieldOffset(Unsafe.java:906)\n     io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.util.UnsafeAccess.fieldOffset(UnsafeAccess.java:107)\n     io.netty.util.internal.shaded.org.jctools.queues.BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueueProducerFields.<clinit>(BaseMpscLinkedArrayQueue.java:55)\n     io.netty.util.internal.PlatformDependent$Mpsc.newChunkedMpscQueue(PlatformDependent.java:1062)\n     io.netty.util.internal.PlatformDependent.newMpscQueue(PlatformDependent.java:1095)\n     io.netty.util.Recycler$LocalPool.<init>(Recycler.java:318)\n     io.netty.util.Recycler$2.initialValue(Recycler.java:111)\n```\n\n19 of 20 tests pass; this one fails.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThat field **is** registered — in `metadata/io.netty/netty-common/4.1.115.Final`. The build did\nnot use that directory. Its own `-H:ConfigurationFileDirectories` shows which one it did use:\n\n```\nmetadata/io.netty/netty-common/5.0.0.Alpha1        <-- selected\nmetadata/io.netty/netty-transport/4.1.115.Final\nmetadata/io.netty/netty-buffer/4.1.80.Final\n...\n```\n\n`metadata/io.netty/netty-common/5.0.0.Alpha1/reachability-metadata.json` contains **zero**\nshaded-jctools entries (netty 5 restructured those classes), so the registration is simply absent\nfrom the image.\n\nThe selection happens because of #9254 (merged 2026-08-15), which moved `\"latest\": true`\n(together with `auto-update` and `high-priority`) off the `4.1.115.Final` entry and onto a new\n`5.0.0.Alpha1` entry:\n\n```diff\n [\n+  {\n+    \"latest\" : true,\n+    \"auto-update\" : true,\n+    \"high-priority\" : true,\n+    \"metadata-version\" : \"5.0.0.Alpha1\",\n+    \"tested-versions\" : [ \"5.0.0.Alpha1\" ],\n...\n   {\n-    \"latest\" : true,\n-    \"auto-update\" : true,\n-    \"high-priority\" : true,\n     \"override\" : true,\n     \"metadata-version\" : \"4.1.115.Final\",\n```\n\nThe `4.1.115.Final` entry's `tested-versions` runs `4.1.115.Final` … `4.1.130.Final` and then the\n4.2.x line. **`4.1.131.Final` and `4.1.132.Final` are in no list at all**, so they match no entry\nand fall back to `latest` — which is now the next-major alpha.\n\n`io.netty:netty-transport` is the control case: its `latest` is still the `4.1.115.Final` entry,\nand the same build resolved `metadata/io.netty/netty-transport/4.1.115.Final` correctly.\n\n### Timeline\n\n| Date | Event | pulsar-common:4.2.1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-08-10 | oracle/graal weekly run 31347176307 | ✅ |\n| 2026-08-15 | #9254 merged — `latest` moves to `5.0.0.Alpha1` | |\n| 2026-08-17 | oracle/graal weekly run 31984989117 | ❌ |\n\n### Suggested fix\n\n1. Add `4.1.131.Final` and `4.1.132.Final` (and keep pace going forward) to the `4.1.115.Final`\n   entry's `tested-versions`.\n2. Reconsider marking a next-major **alpha** as `latest`. The fallback is silent — nothing in the\n   build output says \"your 4.1.x metadata request was served netty-5 metadata\"; you only see it by\n   reading `-H:ConfigurationFileDirectories`. Any 4.1.x version that ages past the enumerated list\n   will hit this again, and the failure mode is a run-time crash rather than a build-time warning.\n3. Consider whether a version that matches no `tested-versions` entry should fall back to the\n   nearest **same-major** entry rather than to `latest`.\n\n## System information\n\n- **GraalVM version:** GraalVM CE 25.3.4.1-dev+0.1 (Java 25.0.4.1+0), built from oracle/graal master\n- **Operating system:** Linux\n- **CPU architecture:** AMD64 (x86-64)",
